d for drop less transdermal delivery of pharmaceutically active compounds for the treatment of anterior segment eye disorders; and retinal XR platform to treat age-related macular degeneration, diabetic macular edema, retinal vein occlusion, and other posterior segment retinal diseases. It sells its products to ambulatory surgery centers, hospitals, and physician private practices through a direct sales organization, direct sales subsidiaries, and distributors. The company was formerly known as Transdx, Inc. Glaukos Corporation was incorporated in 1998 and is headquartered in Aliso Viejo, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas William Burns | Chairman & CEO | Age 64 | Compensation: $856,643 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $464K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $58K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Glaukos Corporation is a large-cap healthcare business with a $14.5B market cap on $507M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years and +22% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -29% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 77% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $22M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -43.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 12% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to ac